<!--
  Hand-maintained sitemap for https://teodorlutoiu.com

  WHEN YOU ADD A PAGE, ADD IT HERE BY HAND. Nothing generates or validates this
  file. It is a plain static asset: Vite copies public/ into dist/ untouched, and
  .github/workflows/deployHost.yml rsyncs dist/ to the document root.

  Why hand-authored: this is a plain Vite static build with no route-generation or
  prerender step. src/App.tsx renders a single page and every nav link is an
  in-page #anchor, so the app contributes exactly one indexable URL ("/"). The
  only other HTML documents in the deployed docroot are the two Retro Many Money
  compliance pages under public/. Wiring a sitemap plugin would add a dependency
  to emit three static lines.

  <lastmod> is the date of the last git commit that changed each page's content,
  not the deploy date. Update it when you change a page.

  <changefreq> and <priority> are deliberately omitted: Google ignores both, and
  stale values are worse than absent ones.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">

  <!-- Homepage. The single-page portfolio: index.html + src/. -->
